# Wizard create warm ownership

## Problem

`warmOperatorWizardShell(pluginId)` awaits `ensureWizardHostReady` → workspace
`wizardHost.ensureReady`. Denali historically warmed **create + flat-edit + shared**
UI surfaces in one `Promise.all`, so `/tours/new` paid for flat-edit-only chunks:

- `wizard-flat-edit-chrome-surface`
- `wizard-flat-edit-form-surface`
- `wizard-flat-edit-page-surface`

After flat-edit was split off create warm, create still paid for the **review** half of
`wizardSurfaces` (composite + review imported together). Review chrome is unused until
the operator reaches the review step.

## Decision (ownership split)

| Path | Warm entry | Surfaces owned |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Create `/tours/new` | `warmOperatorWizardShell` → `wizardHost.ensureReady` only | host-adapter, createChrome, createView, operatorUi, labels, **composite only** (via `ensureWizardCompositePackageSurface`) |
| Review step (first paint of `reviewStepId`) | `WorkspaceWizardHost` awaits `ensureGeneratedReviewSurface` | review surface (capability `wizardSurfaces.ensureReady` still publishes composite+review) |
| Flat-edit `…/tours/[id]/edit` | `warmOperatorWizardShell` **then** `ensureFlatEditChromeReady` + `ensureFlatEditFormReady` + `ensureFlatEditPageReady` | shared create set **plus** the three flat-edit Pattern B surfaces |

### Non-goals

- No change to SDK capability **shape** (`wizardSurfaces.ensureReady`, `flatEditChrome|Form|Page.ensureReady` remain).
- No change to `warmOperatorWizardShell` API.
- No change to create/draft lifecycle or createView/createChrome contracts.
- Flat-edit package `ensure*` stay idempotent (cache hit returns existing surface).
- Labels + composite stay on create warm; step-nav validation still falls back to platform summary when Denali review is cold.

### Contract notes

- `wizardHost.ensureReady` must **not** import flat-edit UI surfaces **or** the review UI module (create must stay lean).
- Package helpers split: `ensureWizardCompositePackageSurface` (create warm) vs
  `ensureWizardReviewPackageSurface` (on-demand) vs
  `ensureWizardSurfacesPackageSurface` (capability `ensureReady` = both; TS-4AS-04).
- Flat-edit page client must not mount Ready until the three flat-edit peeks are non-null
  (or equivalent ensures completed). Cached plugin from create warm alone is insufficient.
- Shell must **not** eagerly `ensureGeneratedReviewSurface` on mount; only when
  `activeStep.stepId === reviewStepId`, and review chrome must wait until that ensure resolves.
- Capability bag still exposes per-surface `ensureReady` for on-demand / edit callers.

## Before / after dependency graph

```text
BEFORE (create paid review)
warmOperatorWizardShell
  └─ wizardHost.ensureReady
       ├─ host-adapter
       ├─ createChrome + createView
       ├─ operatorUi + labels
       └─ wizardSurfaces → composite + review   ← create paid review

WorkspaceWizardHost mount
  └─ ensureGeneratedReviewSurface (eager)       ← also forced review warm

AFTER
warmOperatorWizardShell (/tours/new)
  └─ wizardHost.ensureReady
       ├─ host-adapter
       ├─ createChrome + createView
       ├─ operatorUi + labels
       └─ ensureWizardCompositePackageSurface   ← composite only

WorkspaceWizardHost
  ├─ mount: labels + composite ensure (no review)
  └─ when activeStep === reviewStepId:
       await ensureGeneratedReviewSurface
       → capabilities.wizardSurfaces.ensureReady (composite+review; composite cache hit)
       → renderReviewChrome only after review peek non-null

flat-edit page client
  ├─ warmOperatorWizardShell  (shared set above)
  └─ Promise.all(
       ensureFlatEditChromeReady,
       ensureFlatEditFormReady,
       ensureFlatEditPageReady
     )
```

